# OS
.DS_Store

# skill-creator eval workspaces (never ship)
*-workspace/
**/skill-snapshot*/

# project data must NEVER live in the canonical skill repo — these are safety
# patterns in case anything is ever copied in by mistake (the method is portable,
# the machine's state is not). See references/feedback-loop.md.
**/autosound_context.md
**/dsp-state-current*
**/tuning-changelog*
**/audit-trail.md
**/skill-inbox.md
**/depth-advisor-memory.md
**/feedback-[0-9]*.md
**/rew_analitic/
*.mdat
*.pct6
.gstack/

# Python bytecode cache — machine- and interpreter-version specific, regenerated
# on every run. Two versions of the same module (cpython-310 and cpython-312)
# had both been committed; nothing reads a foreign build's cache.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Working arrangements of the author's own sessions — internal process, not part of the method.
CLAUDE.local.md

# A file that can carry a key is ignored wherever it lands (the user's rule, 2026-09-08: if such
# a file can exist it MUST be ignored, so it never reaches GitHub). `.critic-env.example` is a
# template with placeholders and stays tracked -- these are exact basenames. The check behind the
# rule is scripts/secret-scan.py (run by scripts/run-selftests.sh and by the pre-commit hook).
.critic-env
critic-env
